summary:
There is more than one artist with this name, including:

Divorce was a Scottish noise-rock band from Glasgow that split in August 2013;

Divorce was a Greek heavy metal/AOR band;

DIVORCE is an American techno duo based in Los Angeles, CA;

Divorce is a Swedish pop group;

Divorce is a British alt-country group from Nottingham.

Note; Divorce. was an American rock band from Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, influenced by classic emo bands like Braid and Jimmy Eat World.

Divorce was a Scottish noise rock band from Glasgow. The band's eponymous debut album was released in September 2012 via Night School. The band split in August 2013.

Divorce was a Greek heavy metal/AOR band.

DIVORCE is an American techno duo based in Los Angeles, CA.

Divorce is a Swedish pop group.

Divorce is a British alt-country group from Nottingham formed by vocalist and bassist Tiger Cohen-Towell, co-vocalist Felix Mackenzie-Barrow, lead guitarist Adam Peter-Smith, and drummer Kasper Sandstrom.
First releasing music in 2021, the band released the EPs, Get Mean (2022) and Heady Metal (2023). The bands' debut album, Drive To Goldenhammer, was released in 2025. Read more on Last.fm. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.
